# dist/ and vendor/ are generated build output that `npm run verify:build`
# compares byte for byte against a fresh rebuild. Pin them to LF in the working
# tree: on a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true git hands back CRLF, and
# the drift check would then fail locally against a tree CI considers clean.
dist/*.js text eol=lf
vendor/*.js text eol=lf
